## 2. Architecture

```
                  ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
                  │   SIMULATED AGENT TRAFFIC        │
                  │  (quick-commerce merchant)       │
                  │  legit sessions + 6 attack classes│
                  └────────────────┬────────────────┘
                                   │
                  ┌────────────────▼────────────────┐
                  │  LAYER 1 — MANDATE VERIFIER      │  deterministic
                  │  Is this inside granted authority?│  fast · explainable
                  └────────────────┬────────────────┘
                          pass     │     fail → block + reason trail
                                   │
                  ┌────────────────▼────────────────┐
                  │  LAYER 2 — BEHAVIORAL DETECTOR   │  ML
                  │  Does the session *shape* fit?    │  precision/recall
                  └────────────────┬────────────────┘
                          pass     │     anomalous → step-up / hold
                                   │
                  ┌────────────────▼────────────────┐
                  │  LAYER 3 — INTENT INTEGRITY      │  ← your novel core
                  │  Was the goal hijacked?           │
                  └────────────────┬────────────────┘
                                   │
                  ┌────────────────▼────────────────┐
                  │  LAYER 4 — EVIDENCE / RESPONDER  │  LLM
                  │  Dispute packet + liability call  │  → Razorpay disputes API
                  └────────────────┬────────────────┘
                                   │
                  ┌────────────────▼────────────────┐
                  │  MERCHANT CONSOLE (thin UI)      │
                  └─────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Why layered rather than one model:** deterministic checks are fast, free and fully explainable, so they should run first and catch the obvious. ML runs only on what survives. This is how real risk systems are built, and saying so signals maturity. It also means a failure in your ML layer degrades gracefully instead of taking the system down.

