## 7. Honest Risk Register

Know these before a judge finds them.

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| **Synthetic data can't fully prove real-world performance** | State it plainly. Emphasise that your generator encodes documented, cited attack patterns — not invented ones. Report per-class results so limits are visible. |
| **"Razorpay has no agent object"** | Answer it before they ask. The mandate-as-delegated-authority abstraction is deliberate and defensible — say so in the README and the video. |
| **Scope creep across four layers** | Layer 1 is finishable in week 1 and works standalone. Ship depth-first, not breadth-first. |
| **Layer 3 is ambitious** | I1 (semantic divergence) and I4 (beneficiary novelty) are both implementable in days. Start there. |
| **Someone else picks Track 02** | Likely. But almost nobody will build the *intent* layer, because arriving there requires reading injection research most entrants won't touch. Your defensibility is L3, not the track. |
| **Overclaiming vs. Visa/Mastercard** | Never imply you reimplemented TAP. You built the merchant-side layer for the Razorpay/UPI context. Accurate and still impressive. |

